1230
01:07:48,268 --> 01:07:49,236
From what?

1231
01:07:49,403 --> 01:07:50,337
[scoffs]

1232
01:07:52,406 --> 01:07:53,240
Them.

1233
01:07:54,207 --> 01:07:55,309
Them?

1234
01:07:56,443 --> 01:07:58,713
There are people out there
that want to hurt us.

1235
01:07:59,614 --> 01:08:01,683
Those assholes that broke
into our home.

1236
01:08:01,849 --> 01:08:03,350
[sighs]

1237
01:08:03,518 --> 01:08:04,351
[Simon] There are a ton of
other people that are doing--

1238
01:08:04,519 --> 01:08:05,787
Simon, nobody is after us.

1239
01:08:05,954 --> 01:08:07,522
That was a random break-in.

1240
01:08:08,890 --> 01:08:11,191
-You don't understand.
-Understand what?

1241
01:08:11,358 --> 01:08:13,761
That our g-- garage looks like
a goddamn armory?

1242
01:08:13,928 --> 01:08:16,129
You don't understand what's
happening in the world.

1243
01:08:16,296 --> 01:08:19,667
[sighs] Oh, well please,
why don't you enlighten me then?

1244
01:08:22,135 --> 01:08:23,470
No one's looking out for us.

1245
01:08:25,405 --> 01:08:26,941
No one cares about us.

1246
01:08:28,141 --> 01:08:29,944
The cops aren't doing anything.

1247
01:08:31,278 --> 01:08:32,446
They didn't arrest anyone.

1248
01:08:33,781 --> 01:08:35,415
No one was held accountable.

1249
01:08:36,450 --> 01:08:38,653
It's fucking chaos out there,

1250
01:08:38,820 --> 01:08:41,421
and no one is
doing anything about it.

1251
01:08:41,589 --> 01:08:43,057
[Rebecca] What?

1252
01:08:43,223 --> 01:08:46,027
What the fuck are you
talking about, Simon?

1253
01:08:46,193 --> 01:08:47,929
We just have to be prepared,
that's all.

1254
01:08:50,098 --> 01:08:52,934
Okay, this conversation is
starting to scare me.

1255
01:08:53,101 --> 01:08:55,302
Good. You should be scared.

1256
01:08:55,469 --> 01:08:57,672
Everyone should be scared.

1257
01:08:57,839 --> 01:08:59,641
Everyone should be
fucking terrified.

1258
01:08:59,807 --> 01:09:00,808
-No.
-That's the truth.

1259
01:09:00,975 --> 01:09:02,476
Simon, no.
I'm not going to live in fear.

1260
01:09:02,644 --> 01:09:03,811
All right?
Fear is not good.

1261
01:09:03,978 --> 01:09:05,245
Get rid of them.

1262
01:09:07,081 --> 01:09:08,683
I'm not gonna do that.
They're Gary's.

1263
01:09:08,850 --> 01:09:09,817
[Rebecca sighs]

1264
01:09:13,286 --> 01:09:14,789
I'm pregnant, Simon.

1265
01:09:17,290 --> 01:09:18,860
You have a child coming,

1266
01:09:19,027 --> 01:09:21,129
and I am not raising them
around this.

1267
01:09:26,433 --> 01:09:27,501
What?

1268
01:09:29,837 --> 01:09:31,673
[Rebecca]
I'm about six weeks along.

1269
01:09:32,807 --> 01:09:35,208
I-- [sighs]

1270
01:09:35,375 --> 01:09:36,376
I was gonna tell you
when I found out,

1271
01:09:36,544 --> 01:09:37,712
but then Gary.

1272
01:09:46,486 --> 01:09:47,522
No, it's okay.

1273
01:09:47,689 --> 01:09:49,123
I'll get rid of them.

1274
01:09:50,390 --> 01:09:52,794
-I'll get rid of them.
-[Rebecca sighs] Thank you.

1275
01:09:54,796 --> 01:09:55,997
[Rebecca sighs]

1276
01:09:57,464 --> 01:09:58,166
[Dalton on radio]
<i>I've talked about this before,</i>

1277
01:09:58,331 --> 01:09:59,701
<i>and I'll say it again.</i>

1278
01:09:59,867 --> 01:10:02,537
<i>The 308 is the best all-around</i>
<i>cartridge</i>

1279
01:10:02,704 --> 01:10:05,006
<i>for most shooters'</i>
<i>and hunters' needs.</i>

1280
01:10:05,173 --> 01:10:06,174
[Pete on radio]
<i>Yeah, it's good.</i>

1281
01:10:06,339 --> 01:10:07,675
<i>I like it.</i>

1282
01:10:07,842 --> 01:10:09,677
[Dalton on radio]
<i>It's reliable out to 800 yards.</i>

1283
01:10:09,844 --> 01:10:12,647
<i>It can be kind of expensive,</i>
<i>but--</i>

1284
01:10:12,814 --> 01:10:14,582
[Pete on radio]
<i>It's not that expensive anymore.</i>

1285
01:10:14,749 --> 01:10:16,551
[Dalton on radio] <i>Well, the</i>
<i>rounds I buy can be expensive,</i>

1286
01:10:18,086 --> 01:10:21,455
<i>but what you're buying shows up</i>
<i>on target, 'cause it's accurate.</i>

1287
01:10:21,622 --> 01:10:24,257
[Pete on radio] <i>Yeah, it is.</i>
<i>It is very accurate.</i>

1288
01:10:24,424 --> 01:10:25,927
<i>I got my first elk with a 308.</i>

1289
01:10:26,094 --> 01:10:27,895
<i>I was up in uh, where was I?</i>

1290
01:10:28,062 --> 01:10:30,531
<i>Colville National Forest,</i>
<i>Washington.</i>

1291
01:10:30,698 --> 01:10:32,232
<i>Really pretty country up there.</i>

1292
01:10:33,601 --> 01:10:34,434
[Dalton on radio]
<i>If you're just tuning in,</i>

1293
01:10:34,602 --> 01:10:35,937
<i>we're with Pete Richardson,</i>

1294
01:10:36,104 --> 01:10:39,107
<i>world-renowned sportsman,</i>
<i>hunter guide, novelist,</i>

1295
01:10:39,272 --> 01:10:40,708
<i>and all-around badass.</i>

1296
01:10:40,875 --> 01:10:42,910
[Pete laughs]
<i>Well, thanks for having me.</i>

1297
01:10:43,077 --> 01:10:44,812
[Dalton on radio]
<i>Thanks for being here.</i>

1298
01:10:44,979 --> 01:10:47,247
<i>So tell us, what goes through</i>
<i>the mind of a big game hunter?</i>

1299
01:10:48,683 --> 01:10:50,785
<i>What are you thinking about</i>
<i>out there?</i>

1300
01:10:50,952 --> 01:10:52,620
[Pete on radio] <i>There's</i>
<i>a lot to being a successful</i>

1301
01:10:52,787 --> 01:10:54,021
<i>big game hunter,</i>

1302
01:10:54,188 --> 01:10:57,925
<i>but I think at its core</i>
<i>it's the understanding</i>

1303
01:10:58,092 --> 01:11:00,561
<i>and recognition of patience.</i>

1304
01:11:00,728 --> 01:11:01,596
<i>You have to have patience.</i>

1305
01:11:01,763 --> 01:11:03,698
<i>You can't rush anything.</i>

1306
01:11:03,865 --> 01:11:05,265
<i>Tracking takes time, you know?</i>

1307
01:11:05,432 --> 01:11:06,834
<i>Days, weeks.</i>

1308
01:11:07,001 --> 01:11:10,071
<i>It's knowing when to take that</i>
<i>shot, give yourself the best</i>

1309
01:11:10,238 --> 01:11:12,140
<i>chance to take down</i>
<i>that 10-point.</i>

1310
01:11:12,305 --> 01:11:14,642
<i>I mean, if you wanna get into</i>
<i>the Boone and Crockett Club,</i>

1311
01:11:14,809 --> 01:11:18,780
<i>it's gonna take time and um,</i>
<i>setting yourself up</i>

1312
01:11:18,946 --> 01:11:20,782
<i>for that perfect moment.</i>

1313
01:11:20,948 --> 01:11:23,316
[Dalton on radio]
<i>One shot, one kill.</i>

1314
01:11:23,483 --> 01:11:24,585
[Pete on radio] <i>Oh, yes.</i>

1315
01:11:24,752 --> 01:11:26,286
<i>Yes, I'm a student of</i>
<i>the muzzleloader.</i>

1316
01:11:27,320 --> 01:11:28,321
<i>One shot.</i>

1317
01:11:32,126 --> 01:11:33,060
[intense music playing]

1318
01:11:33,227 --> 01:11:37,632
-[rain pattering]
-[thunder cracking]

1319
01:12:04,424 --> 01:12:05,293
[car door opens]

1320
01:12:12,266 --> 01:12:13,167
[car door closes]

1321
01:12:18,306 --> 01:12:22,677
