1325
01:13:03,084 --> 01:13:03,951
[exhales]

1326
01:13:04,118 --> 01:13:08,155
[panting]

1327
01:13:28,441 --> 01:13:31,779
[munching]

1328
01:13:31,946 --> 01:13:32,780
You okay?

1329
01:13:34,115 --> 01:13:35,082
Yeah.

1330
01:13:37,251 --> 01:13:38,352
Are you nervous?

1331
01:13:41,022 --> 01:13:42,023
No.

1332
01:13:50,665 --> 01:13:51,766
Don't be nervous.

1333
01:13:56,304 --> 01:13:57,405
I'm not.

1334
01:14:08,082 --> 01:14:08,983
[nurse] There we are.

1335
01:14:10,885 --> 01:14:13,421
And there's an arm.

1336
01:14:13,587 --> 01:14:14,655
[chuckles]

1337
01:14:16,791 --> 01:14:17,792
[nurse] A foot.

1338
01:14:17,959 --> 01:14:18,893
[Rebecca laughs]

1339
01:14:20,027 --> 01:14:22,063
[nurse]
Do you wanna know the sex?

1340
01:14:22,229 --> 01:14:23,164
[Rebecca]
No, we wanna wait.

1341
01:14:24,865 --> 01:14:26,434
[nurse]
Do you wanna hear the heartbeat?

1342
01:14:26,600 --> 01:14:28,336
[nurse chuckles]

1343
01:14:29,469 --> 01:14:32,540
[heart thumping]

1344
01:14:32,707 --> 01:14:33,774
[Rebecca laughs]

1345
01:14:33,941 --> 01:14:35,977
[tense music playing]

1346
01:14:36,143 --> 01:14:37,011
[Rebecca] Simon.

1347
01:14:38,980 --> 01:14:40,014
Simon.

1348
01:14:42,984 --> 01:14:43,985
Simon.

1349
01:14:46,120 --> 01:14:47,188
It's amazing.

1350
01:14:47,355 --> 01:14:48,189
It's--

1351
01:14:48,356 --> 01:14:49,857
I'm so happy.

1352
01:14:50,024 --> 01:14:52,326
[laughs]

1353
01:14:59,300 --> 01:15:03,037
[TV playing]

1354
01:15:08,376 --> 01:15:09,643
[Simon]
<i>Thanks for being a voice.</i>

1355
01:15:14,281 --> 01:15:17,818
<i>Thanks for being an unafraid</i>
<i>voice that speaks the truth,</i>

1356
01:15:17,985 --> 01:15:19,854
<i>especially in times like these.</i>

1357
01:15:22,957 --> 01:15:24,025
<i>Everything is.</i>

1358
01:15:26,394 --> 01:15:27,895
<i>.everything</i>
<i>is so broken.</i>

1359
01:15:45,012 --> 01:15:46,680
[Dalton on radio] <i>Today, we're</i>
<i>talking about transportation</i>

1360
01:15:46,847 --> 01:15:49,250
<i>and the potential collapse of</i>
<i>this country's backbone.</i>

1361
01:15:50,684 --> 01:15:52,753
<i>What's happening to the</i>
<i>trucking industry?</i>

1362
01:15:54,655 --> 01:15:58,192
<i>Said it before and I'll say</i>
<i>it again, we don't value labor</i>

1363
01:15:58,359 --> 01:15:59,693
<i>anymore in this country.</i>

1364
01:15:59,860 --> 01:16:01,328
<i>We don't.</i>

1365
01:16:01,495 --> 01:16:02,897
<i>Now, I'm not saying</i>
<i>I'm anti-union.</i>

1366
01:16:03,064 --> 01:16:03,998
<i>Quite the contrary.</i>

1367
01:16:04,999 --> 01:16:06,834
<i>But we need a change of focus.</i>

1368
01:16:08,369 --> 01:16:11,605
<i>We need to turn the needle</i>
<i>back, get away from all this--</i>

1369
01:16:11,772 --> 01:16:13,040
<i>this automation.</i>

1370
01:16:14,208 --> 01:16:16,944
<i>These robots are gonna drive us</i>
<i>to an early extinction,</i>

1371
01:16:17,111 --> 01:16:18,112
<i>I'm telling you.</i>

1372
01:16:20,581 --> 01:16:24,885
[machinery whirring]

1373
01:16:31,526 --> 01:16:32,527
[Will] Simon.

1374
01:16:37,532 --> 01:16:38,732
[knocking on door]

1375
01:16:38,899 --> 01:16:43,437
[door opens and closes]

1376
01:16:45,072 --> 01:16:48,209
Simon, this is Officer
Bondurant, Officer Sherman.

1377
01:16:49,777 --> 01:16:51,145
They got a few questions
for you.

1378
01:16:53,280 --> 01:16:56,150
Mr. Ward, we had a report filed
that you accosted a Peter Ellis

1379
01:16:56,317 --> 01:16:58,152
over at the WFBX studios.

1380
01:16:58,319 --> 01:16:59,487
-[laughs]
-That true?

1381
01:16:59,653 --> 01:17:00,821
No.

1382
01:17:00,988 --> 01:17:02,223
You didn't get into
a physical altercation?

1383
01:17:02,389 --> 01:17:03,157
No.

1384
01:17:03,324 --> 01:17:04,925
It was a misunderstanding and--

1385
01:17:05,092 --> 01:17:07,761
[Officer Sherman] Mr. Ellis
isn't pressing charges,

1386
01:17:07,928 --> 01:17:09,830
but the station filed
a restraining order against you.

1387
01:17:11,499 --> 01:17:12,967
You just can't go near
the properties anymore.

1388
01:17:15,436 --> 01:17:17,471
It's best to probably avoid it
altogether.

1389
01:17:17,638 --> 01:17:20,674
[laughs]

1390
01:17:20,841 --> 01:17:22,643
What's the charge?

1391
01:17:22,810 --> 01:17:24,345
We're not charging you.

1392
01:17:24,513 --> 01:17:25,614
It's a restraining order.

1393
01:17:27,081 --> 01:17:28,517
Look, just stay away
from the property

1394
01:17:28,682 --> 01:17:29,984
and you won't be in violation.

1395
01:17:32,453 --> 01:17:33,654
You got any questions for us?

1396
01:17:36,690 --> 01:17:37,626
All right.

1397
01:17:37,791 --> 01:17:39,160
Well, we appreciate it, fellas.

1398
01:17:39,326 --> 01:17:41,128
We'll let you get back to it.
You guys have a great day.

1399
01:17:41,295 --> 01:17:42,263
Thank you, guys.

1400
01:17:43,297 --> 01:17:44,533
[door opens]

1401
01:17:48,135 --> 01:17:48,936
[door closes]

1402
01:17:50,304 --> 01:17:54,141
Simon, what's this all about?

1403
01:17:54,308 --> 01:17:55,376
Nothing.

1404
01:17:55,544 --> 01:17:56,844
It doesn't matter.

1405
01:17:57,011 --> 01:17:58,179
It doesn't matter?

1406
01:17:58,345 --> 01:17:59,947
Guy was a fucking jerk,
all right?

1407
01:18:00,114 --> 01:18:02,316
And now I'm gonna pay the price
for it.

1408
01:18:03,350 --> 01:18:05,953
Simon, listen, buddy, you need
some time to refocus here.

1409
01:18:08,122 --> 01:18:09,290
I'm serious.

1410
01:18:10,991 --> 01:18:13,394
When the cops have to come
to your work and serve you

1411
01:18:13,562 --> 01:18:15,462
with a restraining order?

1412
01:18:15,630 --> 01:18:17,198
[chuckles]

1413
01:18:17,364 --> 01:18:20,034
Simon, I don't wanna fire you,
buddy,

1414
01:18:20,201 --> 01:18:21,168
but I am taking you off
the schedule for the time being.

1415
01:18:21,335 --> 01:18:22,671
I can't take time.

1416
01:18:22,836 --> 01:18:24,738
-[Will] Until you refocus--
-I have a baby coming.

1417
01:18:26,207 --> 01:18:28,643
-Okay? I can't take time.
-Well, this ain't voluntary.

1418
01:18:28,809 --> 01:18:31,145
This isn't right.
I didn't do anything.

1419
01:18:31,312 --> 01:18:33,747
Can you not see I'm tossing you
a lifeline here?

1420
01:18:36,750 --> 01:18:37,818
Buddy, I get it.

1421
01:18:39,019 --> 01:18:40,555
I do, I understand.

1422
01:18:42,990 --> 01:18:44,758
But I also think
this is what's best.

1423
01:18:46,060 --> 01:18:46,927
Mm-hmm.

1424
01:18:48,262 --> 01:18:49,598
I'll get Sal to cover for you.

1425
01:18:49,763 --> 01:18:50,565
No.

1426
01:18:52,166 --> 01:18:53,100
No.

1427
01:18:54,569 --> 01:18:56,403
Fuck you. I quit.

1428
01:18:57,738 --> 01:18:58,939
-Simon.
-What?

1429
01:18:59,106 --> 01:18:59,873
Huh?

1430
01:19:00,040 --> 01:19:01,041
What?

1431
01:19:04,178 --> 01:19:05,079
Simon.

1432
01:19:06,615 --> 01:19:07,414
[door slams shut]

1433
01:19:08,550 --> 01:19:09,750
I'ma need your keys back, man.

1434
01:19:11,553 --> 01:19:14,689
Hey, Ward, look, come on, man,
wait a second.

1435
01:19:14,855 --> 01:19:15,789
Simon, look, look.

1436
01:19:17,626 --> 01:19:18,459
Listen.

1437
01:19:19,426 --> 01:19:20,294
[sighs]

1438
01:19:21,395 --> 01:19:22,697
I'm sorry about Parker,
all right?

1439
01:19:22,863 --> 01:19:26,233
[tense music playing]

1440
01:19:26,400 --> 01:19:27,401
[laughs]

1441
01:19:29,604 --> 01:19:30,572
You disgust me.

1442
01:19:32,072 --> 01:19:33,708
You fucking disgust me.

1443
01:19:35,543 --> 01:19:36,877
What?

1444
01:19:37,044 --> 01:19:37,911
I what?

1445
01:19:40,080 --> 01:19:42,584
[scoffs] I disgust you.

1446
01:19:45,052 --> 01:19:48,590
You ever follow me again
and I will fucking kill you.

1447
01:19:48,757 --> 01:19:49,957
Do you understand?

1448
01:19:50,124 --> 01:19:51,458
I will fucking kill you.

1449
01:19:51,626 --> 01:19:57,464
[♪♪♪]

1450
01:20:08,677 --> 01:20:13,080
[heavy breathing]

1451
01:20:13,247 --> 01:20:14,114
[grunts]

1452
01:20:14,281 --> 01:20:19,186
[cries, panting]

1453
01:20:25,660 --> 01:20:27,928
[car drives off]

1454
01:20:28,095 --> 01:20:33,867
[♪♪♪]

1455
01:21:04,498 --> 01:21:08,869
[gun loading]

1456
01:21:30,424 --> 01:21:31,492
[gunshot]

1457
01:21:31,659 --> 01:21:33,093
[bolt cycles]

1458
01:21:34,596 --> 01:21:35,764
[gunshot]

1459
01:21:35,929 --> 01:21:37,532
[bolt cycles]

1460
01:21:41,034 --> 01:21:44,773
[target carrier whirring]

1461
01:21:59,086 --> 01:22:00,354
[Dalton on radio]
More and more apparent

1462
01:22:00,522 --> 01:22:03,023
that our current political
system is failing us.

1463
01:22:04,526 --> 01:22:07,928
Had a chance to dig into some
13F filing released yesterday.

1464
01:22:09,430 --> 01:22:12,933
A 13F is a financial institution
report, mainly banks.

1465
01:22:13,100 --> 01:22:17,938
We're talking JP Morgan Chase,
Bank of America, PNC, et cetera.

1466
01:22:19,541 --> 01:22:22,409
They report that middle class
savings has dropped

1467
01:22:22,577 --> 01:22:26,079
$3.1 trillion in Q2.

1468
01:22:26,246 --> 01:22:26,947
[Rebecca on voicemail]
<i>Hi, you've reached Rebecca.</i>

1469
01:22:27,114 --> 01:22:28,115
<i>I'm not in right now--</i>

1470
01:22:28,282 --> 01:22:29,651
[Dalton on radio]
<i>Did you hear me, people?</i>

